packages/aqua/aqua-official — 1inch's official Aqua registry, UNMODIFIED (LicenseRef-Degensoft-Aqua-Source-1.1)

What this is
  Noren redeploys 1inch's official Aqua registry (contract AquaRouter = Aqua + Simulator + Multicall)
  on Arc Testnet (chain 5042002). 1inch deployed Aqua at 0x1111113ccf1426a8e30e2bff5e005d929bf6a90a on
  Arc mainnet (5042) through a CREATE3 factory that has no code on Arc Testnet, so that address cannot
  be used there. Noren deployed the same code at its own address. Nothing in Aqua was modified.

Upstream
  github.com/1inch/aqua, tag v1.0.0, commit 81c26e4619ce21556ab02b3284ee2685de21fb18.
  Sources (src/), foundry.toml and remappings.txt are taken from that commit with `git archive`
  and are never edited. Dependencies: @1inch/solidity-utils 6.9.7 and @openzeppelin/contracts 5.4.0,
  the exact versions upstream v1.0.0 pins (MIT; see LICENSES/ and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES).
  LICENSE, LICENSES/ and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES in this folder are copied unchanged from that commit.

Bytecode check (build-check.json)
  The runtime bytecode built from that commit is 5,619 bytes, the same length as the code at
  0x1111113c…a90a on Arc mainnet, and identical to it byte for byte except the 32-byte IPFS hash
  inside the trailing CBOR metadata (that hash covers source paths and file contents of the build
  environment, not the code). Aqua has no immutables. Its one constructor argument is the Rescuable
  owner (storage, not code): it may only rescue tokens sent to the registry contract by mistake and has
  no power over makers' balances or strategies. On Arc mainnet it is 1inch's deployer
  0x0BD61d605C64A857C3D94779aEf7cA295702b3A2; on Noren's Arc Testnet copy it is Noren's deployer.

Build and deploy (reproducible)
  pnpm install                                           # packages/aqua deps (solidity-utils, OZ)
  bash scripts/live/aqua-build-official.sh               # fetch the pinned commit, build, compare
  pnpm exec tsx scripts/live/aqua-live.ts deploy         # CREATE2 (0x4e59b448…956C) on Arc Testnet
  The deploy step recompares the deployed runtime with Arc mainnet's code. Addresses and transactions
  are recorded in packages/xchain-aqua/live/arc-testnet.json and docs/AQUA-LIVE.md.

